        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Under dry N2 using Schlenk techniques, bis-5,5′-(1,3-propanediyldiimino)-2,2-dimethyl-4-hexene-3-one (0.288 g, 0.892 mmol) in 50 mL THF was added to Nd[N(TMS)2]3 (0.558 g, 0.891 mmol) dissolved in 30 mL THF and the mixture was heated at reflux overnight. THF was removed in vacuo, 20 mL pentane was added, and the solution was concentrated in vacuo to about 2 mL. Pale-blue crystals of 8 were harvested from the mother liquor after standing at −18 °C for 1 week. The oxide ligands are attributed to oxygen abstraction from THF at elevated temperature.",
